  "notes": "よす is a casual/colloquial verb meaning to stop or quit an action. Common in informal speech.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle: タバコをよす (quit smoking)\n\nREGISTER:\nCasual to rough. Often used in commands or strong suggestions. Not appropriate in formal settings.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- よせ! / よせよ!: Stop it! (imperative, rough)\n- よしなさい: Stop that (softer command, often to children)\n- ～をよした{方|ほう}がいい: You'd better quit ~\n- よそう: Let's stop / I'll stop (volitional)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- やめる: to stop, quit (more neutral, widely usable)\n- {止|と}める: to stop (more formal, also physical stopping)",
